    "description": "Iran’s vegetation ranges from humid Caspian forests to dry mountain woodland, plateau shrublands, highland pastures, and tidal mangroves. Climate, elevation, soils, and human land use help explain both this diversity and the different conservation challenges facing each landscape.",
    "tags": ["Forests", "Vegetation", "Hyrcanian forests", "Zagros", "Rangelands", "Mangroves", "Plant diversity"],
    "status": null,
